# API documentation synchronization

Whenever an API endpoint is created, modified, renamed, or removed, inspect `documentation/api/openapi.yaml`.

## Required practice

- Update the OpenAPI specification in the same development task whenever the API contract changes.
- Keep request schemas, response schemas, parameters, validation behavior, status codes, and error responses synchronized with the implementation.
- Do not document behavior that the API does not actually implement.
- Do not modify API behavior merely to make the documentation match unless explicitly requested.
- API tests and OpenAPI documentation should be updated together when an API contract changes.
- Before completing API-related work, validate that the OpenAPI documentation matches the implementation and tests.

## Scope

This rule applies to all future API work in this project, not only the Place API.
